{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "curated_at": "2026-05-12",
  "purpose": "Calibration ground truth for the Resistance Atlas (RA spike #1). Every entry is a published (target, mutation, drug) event where mutation-driven binding shift has been documented in the clinical or pre-clinical literature. Used to (1) measure how much of clinical resistance Liganx's Δ-from-rigid-docking alone recovers, and (2) train the calibration layer that triangulates Δ + ESM2 fitness + codon accessibility into a forecast probability.",
  "methodology_notes": [
    "wt_residue + position + mutant uses standard one-letter codes; position is the canonical UniProt residue number (NOT the PDB residue number — those differ for several catalog entries because chain renumbering varies across crystals).",
    "codon_distance is the minimum number of single-nucleotide changes required to convert the WT codon to a codon encoding the mutant amino acid, using the standard genetic code. 1 = single-nucleotide-accessible (much more likely to emerge clinically); 2-3 = multi-step (rarer).",
    "mechanism categorises the structural pathway by which the mutation alters drug binding. Liganx's rigid-receptor docking sees gatekeeper / steric / P-loop reshape strongly; covalent_escape and conformational_shift are weakly recovered (documented method limits on /validation).",
    "expected_direction is the clinical outcome: 'resistance' = drug loses potency vs WT; 'selectivity' = drug gains potency vs WT (e.g. allele-selective designs like Sotorasib, Vemurafenib); 'retained' = drug holds potency despite the mutation (e.g. Pirtobrutinib vs C481S).",
    "smiles strings come from backend/data/libraries/oncology_kinase_inhibitors_v1.json (RDKit-validated 2026-05-12). Sotorasib/Adagrasib/Tucatinib were also re-verified vs PubChem CIDs after the May 2026 audit.",
    "Pre-clinical events (Phase I/II resistance in published papers) are included alongside clinically-emerged events; we tag clinical_emergence=true when the mutation has been documented in patient samples from late-line therapy, false when it's only been reported from cell-line / mutagenesis screens. The forecast model treats both as positive examples but the latter as lower-weight."
  ],
